{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:22992589 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:22992589 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"22992589","source":"MED","pmid":"22992589","pmcid":"PMC3985763","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3985763"]},"doi":"10.1038/nrm3432","title":"Assembly of allosteric macromolecular switches: lessons from PKA.","authorString":"Taylor SS, Ilouz R, Zhang P, Kornev AP.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Taylor SS","lastName":"Taylor","firstName":"Susan S","initials":"SS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pharmacology, University of California, San Diego, La Jolla, 92093-90654, USA. staylor@ucsd.edu"}]}},{"fullName":"Ilouz R","lastName":"Ilouz","firstName":"Ronit","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Zhang P","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Ping","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0340-281X"}},{"fullName":"Kornev AP","lastName":"Kornev","firstName":"Alexandr P","initials":"AP","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1543-3795"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0340-281X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1543-3795"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"10","volume":"13","journalIssueId":1968279,"dateOfPublication":"2012 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2012,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Nat Rev Mol Cell Biol","title":"Nature reviews. Molecular cell biology","essn":"1471-0080","issn":"1471-0072","nlmid":"100962782","isoabbreviation":"Nat Rev Mol Cell Biol"},"printPublicationDate":"2012-10-01"},"pubYear":"2012","pageInfo":"646-658","abstractText":"Protein kinases are dynamic molecular switches that have evolved to be only transiently activated. Kinase activity is embedded within a conserved kinase core, which is typically regulated by associated domains, linkers and interacting proteins. Moreover, protein kinases are often tethered to large macromolecular complexes to provide tighter spatiotemporal control. Thus, structural characterization of kinase domains alone is insufficient to explain protein kinase function and regulation in vivo. Recent progress in structural characterization of cyclic AMP-dependent protein kinase (PKA) exemplifies how our knowledge of kinase signalling has evolved by shifting the focus of structural studies from single kinase subunits to macromolecular complexes.","affiliation":"Department of Pharmacology, University of California, San Diego, La Jolla, 92093-90654, USA. staylor@ucsd.edu","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Review","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"R01 GM019301","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"R01 GM034921","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","grantId":"DK54441","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","grantId":"P01 DK054441","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"R37 GM019301","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM34921","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","acronym":"HHMI","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM19301","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Macromolecular Substances","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclic AMP-Dependent Protein Kinases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chem